[[Image:BrawlerT.png|left]]''<font style="font-size:12px">{{Quote|Up close and personal: that's how Brawlers like it! Rough and rugged, they always mean business and are up for fight anytime with anyone. Brawlers are tough stuff! They use hammers, clubs, and powerful kicks to defeat enemies no matter how large or scary. You can learn to be a Brawler during the tutorial, and there is a Brawler trainer in every starting area.|Job description}}</font>''
<br />
'''Brawler''' is a combat [[Jobs|job]], specializing in close combat utilizing blunt weapons like hammers. A combat class job, experience is gained by completing Brawler [[Quests|quests]] and by battling in combat instances in the [[Wilds]] and in [[Dungeons|dungeons]].

==Restrictions - Job Change==
Recently, since the opening of [[Sunstone Valley]], as of March 16, 2012, non-[[Membership|members]] can also max out the Brawler job.

==Starting the Brawler Questline==
The Brawler questline can be started with any of the following trainers:
* Flanders in the [[Sacred Glade]] tutorial (no longer in-game)
* Harold in [[Highroad Junction]]
* Carlos Brazenfist in [[Cobblestone Village]]
* Caitlyn Gravefog in [[Stillwater Crossing]]

==Trainers==
* Flanders in the Sacred Glade tutorial (starts questline; No longer in-game)
